comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T17:19:35.295Z","harness:claude-code","Direct confirmation of this item's thesis, captured 2026-07-26 at the moment it mattered most.\n\nImmediately before the terminal relationship backfill, graph audit --summary reported isolated_active_nodes 0 and degree_leq_one_active_nodes 0, with every per-type coverage bucket clean, over active_nodes 293 of nodes 2091. At that same instant, direct measurement over the .toon corpus showed 1,024 of 1,795 terminal items with no outbound edge and 822 with no edge in either direction. The audit was not wrong about what it measured; it certified a graph that was 86 percent unmeasured and reported no signal that it had done so.\n\nThat is the conformance gap against pm-6x7o's acceptance criterion that coverage profiles vary by lifecycle state. The fix direction this suggests: report coverage per lifecycle state as separate profiles with their own denominators, and make the absence of a terminal profile a finding rather than a silence. A single all-clear over an active-only denominator is actively misleading, because it is indistinguishable from an all-clear over everything.\n"
  "2026-07-28T10:04:18.406Z","harness:claude-code","All-status connectivity census, 2026-07-28, measured directly from the 2,159 tracked item documents rather than from the audit, because the audit reports only the active slice this item exists to widen.\n\nDegree here counts inbound typed dependency edges plus outbound typed dependency edges plus the parent edge.\n\n  status     items   deg1   deg2   deg3-5   deg6-10   deg11-25   deg26+\n  open         306      0      0       50        97        102       57\n  closed     1,840      9    220      808       497        256       50\n  canceled      13      0      0        6         7          0        0\n\nFindings that only an all-status census produces:\n\nZero isolates at any status. The active-scoped audit reports 0 isolated and 0 degree-leq-one active nodes and is correct; the same holds for the 1,853 terminal nodes it never measures. The saturation the audit certifies turns out to be real beyond its own scope, which is worth recording because it was not knowable from the audit.\n\nThe thin tail is terminal and it is small. 229 closed items sit at degree 2 or below and 9 sit at degree 1. That is 12.4 percent of closed items in the bottom two buckets against 0 percent of open items, which is the expected shape -- active work accumulates edges while it is worked -- but it is a measurable gradient the current metric cannot express at all.\n\nOnly 8 closed items carry no typed dependency edge whatsoever, reaching the graph through their parent and through inbound edges alone. They were individually inspected and repaired this session where the item's own recorded resolution supplied the evidence: pm-gjicmx, the single least-connected node in the workspace, is now linked into the merge-safety lineage its resolution describes; pm-mp49 and pm-v657 are linked as the sibling package defects they are; pm-hybj is linked into the changelog lineage it originated.\n\nWhat this argues for the metric. A coverage number scoped to actives cannot distinguish a workspace whose history is richly linked from one whose history is a flat list under a parent, and both certify identically today. The census above is cheap -- one pass over the item documents -- and the degree histogram per status is more informative than the isolate count it would replace, because the isolate count is already zero and will stay zero while the distribution underneath it is still free to degrade.\n"
  "2026-07-29T04:34:40.414Z","harness:claude-code","Sibling measured 2026-07-29: the same lifecycle-scoping question is answered three different ways by three governance surfaces and no rule states which is correct. graph audit scopes coverage metrics to active nodes and under-reports (this item). validate --check-files scopes to every holder and over-reports 1,220 links that are all on closed items, warning forever (pm-zw9188). validate dependency_references partitions into active, legacy-closed and legacy-terminal counters and reports ok when active is empty - the only one of nine validate checks with a lifecycle dimension, and the only one that ever went green. Whatever principle resolves this item should be stated once and applied to all three, not decided per surface."
  "2026-07-31T06:14:45.475Z","harness:claude-code","All-status measurement 2026-07-31, computed directly from the stored dependency arrays rather than from the audit profile, so the active-node scoping this item reports is bypassed. Terminal population 1,904: nine nodes at degree one or less, 228 at degree two or less, zero isolates. Kind diversity across all 2,226 nodes: nine nodes carry exactly one edge kind, 360 carry two, 1,245 carry three, 428 four, 143 five, 30 six, four seven. Typed reachability to an outcome milestone over non-related kinds only: every node reaches one within five hops, terminal included. So the unmeasured terminal population is in materially better shape than the missing metric implies — the deficiency is ordering, not connectivity."
  "2026-09-07T06:11:51.537Z","harness:codex","Implementation design: add lifecycle and raw-status connectivity/semantic coverage with declared denominators; preserve active-only compatibility counters; retain historical cycle severity policy and expose structural acyclicity separately so warning policy does not falsify graph correctness. Parent notes explicitly require informational terminal-only legacy cycles, so this conflicts with the older blanket severity criterion and will be documented with evidence."
  "2026-09-07T06:24:12.314Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: initial regression suite passes locally; integration, additional edge cases, full coverage and release/review gates remain underway. No delivery or release completion claimed."
  "2026-09-07T06:48:03.067Z","harness:codex","Live graph census now measures 2652 recorded nodes and 13059 directed edges: 276 active and 2376 terminal, zero isolates or degree-at-most-one nodes in either population. Semantic incidence is 153 active and 952 terminal nodes; 1424 terminal nodes have no provenance/verification incidence. All 2376 terminal nodes reach an outcome through the separately declared typed reachability basis. This identifies measured historical enrichment scope without fabricating graph edges or claiming relationship saturation from active-only counters."
  "2026-09-07T07:11:57.196Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: complete 8521-test run passed; exact coverage exposed one census guard branch, and an added custom-status regression caught inherited-property collisions for constructor and __proto__ in signed baseline deltas. Comparison now resolves own status keys only. Bounded summary emits lifecycle connectivity totals while full restores distributions; a real workspace test proves summary baseline saves retain full raw-status and degree measurements. Token-budget gate passed all 32 surfaces without changing ceilings."
  "2026-09-07T07:45:33.417Z","harness:codex","Local implementation verification: exact full-source coverage passed at 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (60671 lines, 63170 statements, 13078 functions, 47962 branches). The full run had one stale workspace-intent assertion; that expected text was synchronized, then all 55 contracts and aggregation acceptance tests passed. Full static quality, context-quality and 56 token surfaces, typecheck, linked tests, staged secret scan, latest-release compatibility migration, 88-command package dogfood, installed npm/Bun CLI/SDK/MCP acceptance, and packed npx/bunx smoke passed. Hosted exact-head review, merge, and publication remain separate delivery steps; no hosted or released state is claimed here."
  "2026-09-07T08:00:16.111Z","harness:codex","Hosted review correction: the first Gates (static) run rejected missing escape_class and gate_evidence after implementation closure. Both fields now identify the production behavior gap and the real regression suite that failed before the fix. No gate policy or exemption was changed. Full final local run passed all 8523 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-09-07T08:25:14.440Z","harness:codex","Delivery attribution correction: the earlier close recorded preliminary implementation completion before the independently scheduled v2026.9.7 tag, but that immutable tag does not contain this branch. Final integration of the release base, completed review handling, current static gates, and installed branch acceptance completed after the tag. Correct completed_at to this final integration completion so package-owned history retains this work under Unreleased. The earlier close event remains preserved."
  "2026-09-07T08:32:34.016Z","harness:codex","Final connected-delivery verification: all 8524 tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100, full static gates and installed branch npm/Bun CLI/SDK/MCP acceptance pass. Review corrections are included before the final hosted round. Immutable daily v2026.9.7 publication and installed consumers also pass separately; this branch remains Unreleased. No open GitHub issues or dependency/security alerts were returned by the latest complete inventories."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T07:26:15.341Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle census denominators must include historical work even when finding severity exempts legacy debt. Persist full measurements behind compact output projections, and treat absent legacy metrics as incomparable."
